{
  "slug": "project-setup",
  "name": "Project Setup",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Automatically configures .claude/ by reading your existing project files. Detects Python venvs, Node.js,  Rust, and Go toolchains, plus linters, test runners, and IDE settings (VSCode, PyCharm, Vim, Emacs). No manual setup required.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills**, **3 commands** and **2 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (6): `detect-directories` (Discover additional source directories outside the project root that should be accessible), `detect-environment` (Detect language runtimes, virtual environments, and toolchains (Python, Node, Rust, Go)), `detect-ide-settings` (Read IDE/editor configuration files (VSCode, PyCharm, Vim/Neovim, Emacs) to discover project settings), `detect-linters` (Detect linters and formatters configured in the project across Python, JS/TS, Rust, and Go), `detect-runtime-context` (Detect whether the project is running locally or in a remote/container environment (GitHub Codespaces, VS Code Dev Containers,…), `detect-test-runners` (Detect test runners and testing configuration across Python, JS/TS, Rust, and Go)\n- **Commands** (3): `check` (Validate that .claude/ configuration is correct and functional), `copy-from` (Copy and adapt .claude/ configuration from another project), `project-setup` (Auto-discover project tooling and configure .claude/ settings)\n- **Hooks** (2): `SessionStart`, `CwdChanged`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install project-setup@claude-community` from `lambdao-dev/claude-project-setup-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 6,
    "hook": 2,
    "command": 3
  },
